IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `spr-dates`
IMPORT `spr-nouns`

-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173), revised text at 2026-04-06.
--
-- LAYER 1, PART 3: regulations 4 to 12A (deferral of state pension).
-- Written from the text alone and from no one's point of view.
--
-- "Deferral" means putting off the start of the state pension, or (suspension)
-- pausing it, in return for a bigger pension later. The parent Act (the Pensions Act
-- 2014, ss 8, 9 and 17) is not among the inputs. Where a regulation leans on it, the
-- effect of the Act is taken as a stated input and the module says so at that place:
--   * "falls within section 8(1)" is a fact (regulations 4 and 5);
--   * the amounts of a lump sum and of a section 9 pension are inputs (regulation 6);
--   * how section 17(3) and (4) turn weeks and a percentage into an increase is
--     taken as: increase per week = specified percentage times the reference weekly
--     rate (regulation 12A(2) states the multiplication by the percentage).

§ `Part 3: Deferral of State Pension`

§§ `Regulation 4: when a choice of lump sum or survivor's pension may be made`

DECLARE ChoicePeriodFacts HAS
    `the person falls within section 8(1) of the 2014 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date in the most recent notice, issued before the choice was made, confirming that the person may make the choice, if any` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date the person claims a state pension` IS A DATE
    `the date the person's spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE
    `the date the person makes the choice` IS A DATE

DECLARE ChoicePeriod HAS
    `the first day of the period for the choice` IS A DATE
    `the last day of the period for the choice` IS A DATE

DECLARE ChoiceTiming IS ONE OF
    `the choice is within the period`
    `the choice is outside the period`
    `regulation 4 does not cover the person`

-- Gloss: where the Secretary of State has sent a notice, the person has three months
-- from the date in the notice (the latest notice, if there are several).
-- Three months "starting on" a date is counted by convention F2 (NOTES.md).
-- src:50 | (2) Where the Secretary of State has issued a notice which confirms that the person may make the choice, the period is three months starting on the date in that notice (or, where there is more than one notice which confirms that the person may make that choice, the date in the most recent such notice).
@ref Regulation 4(2) (src:50)
GIVEN noticeDate IS A DATE
GIVETH A ChoicePeriod
`regulation 4(2): the period for the choice where a notice has been issued` noticeDate MEANS
    ChoicePeriod WITH
        `the first day of the period for the choice` IS noticeDate
        `the last day of the period for the choice` IS `the last day of a period of months starting on` noticeDate 3

-- Gloss: where the person chooses before any notice, the period runs from the later of
-- the date they claim a state pension and the date their spouse or civil partner died,
-- to the date they make the choice.
-- src:51 | (3) Where the person makes the choice before the Secretary of State has issued any such notice, the period—
-- src:52 | (a) starts on the later of the date—
-- src:53 | (i) the person claims a state pension; or
-- src:54 | (ii) the person's spouse or civil partner died; and
-- src:55 | (b) ends on the date the person makes the choice.
@ref Regulation 4(3) (src:51-55)
GIVEN facts IS A ChoicePeriodFacts
GIVETH A ChoicePeriod
`regulation 4(3): the period for the choice where the person chooses before any notice` facts MEANS
    ChoicePeriod WITH
        `the first day of the period for the choice` IS
            IF facts's `the date the person claims a state pension` GREATER THAN facts's `the date the person's spouse or civil partner died`
            THEN facts's `the date the person claims a state pension`
            ELSE facts's `the date the person's spouse or civil partner died`
        `the last day of the period for the choice` IS facts's `the date the person makes the choice`

-- src:47 | (1) Where a person falls within section 8(1) of the 2014 Act (choice of lump sum or survivor's pension under section 9 in certain cases), paragraphs (2) and (3) set out the period within which that person is to make any choice under section 8(2) of that Act to be paid—
-- src:48 | (a) a lump sum under section 8 of that Act; or
-- src:49 | (b) a state pension under section 9 of that Act (survivor's pension based on inheritance of deferred old state pension).
@ref Regulation 4(1) (src:47-49)
GIVEN facts IS A ChoicePeriodFacts
GIVETH A MAYBE ChoicePeriod
`regulation 4(1): the period within which the person is to make the choice` facts MEANS
    IF NOT (facts's `the person falls within section 8(1) of the 2014 Act`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER facts's `the date in the most recent notice, issued before the choice was made, confirming that the person may make the choice, if any`
         WHEN JUST noticeDate THEN JUST (`regulation 4(2): the period for the choice where a notice has been issued` noticeDate)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`regulation 4(3): the period for the choice where the person chooses before any notice` facts)

-- Whether the date on which the person makes the choice falls in that period.
@ref Regulation 4(1) (src:47-49)
GIVEN facts IS A ChoicePeriodFacts
GIVETH A ChoiceTiming
`regulation 4: whether the choice is made within the period` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER `regulation 4(1): the period within which the person is to make the choice` facts
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `regulation 4 does not cover the person`
    WHEN JUST period THEN
        IF       facts's `the date the person makes the choice` AT LEAST period's `the first day of the period for the choice`
             AND facts's `the date the person makes the choice` AT MOST period's `the last day of the period for the choice`
        THEN `the choice is within the period`
        ELSE `the choice is outside the period`

DECLARE LateChoiceFacts HAS
    `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8(4) of the 2014 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that amount has been repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Gloss: after the period, a late choice is allowed if the Secretary of State thinks
-- it reasonable in the case AND any lump sum already paid has been repaid in full and
-- in the currency in which it was paid.
-- Where no lump sum has been paid there is nothing to repay, so (b) is met
-- (NOTES.md, fork F11).
-- src:56 | (4) A person may make a late choice after the period set out in this regulation in circumstances where—
-- src:57 | (a) the Secretary of State considers it is reasonable in any particular case; and
-- src:58 | (b) any amount paid by way of (or on account of) a lump sum under section 8(4) of the 2014 Act has been repaid to the Secretary of State—
-- src:59 | (i) in full; and
-- src:60 | (ii) in the currency in which that amount was originally paid.
@ref Regulation 4(4) (src:56-60)
GIVEN facts IS A LateChoiceFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 4(4): a late choice may be made` facts MEANS
        facts's `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular case`
    AND (   NOT (facts's `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8(4) of the 2014 Act`)
         OR (       facts's `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full`
                AND facts's `that amount has been repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid`))

-- Gloss: the lump sum falls to nil where a late choice for the state pension is made.
-- src:61 | (5) The amount of any lump sum to be paid to the person under section 8(4) is reduced to nil where the person makes a late choice under paragraph (4) to be paid a state pension under section 9 of the 2014 Act.
@ref Regulation 4(5) (src:61)
GIVEN `the amount of the lump sum that would otherwise be paid under section 8(4)` IS A NUMBER
      `the person makes a late choice under regulation 4(4) to be paid a state pension under section 9` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 4(5): the amount of the lump sum` `the amount of the lump sum that would otherwise be paid under section 8(4)` `the person makes a late choice under regulation 4(4) to be paid a state pension under section 9` MEANS
    IF `the person makes a late choice under regulation 4(4) to be paid a state pension under section 9`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the amount of the lump sum that would otherwise be paid under section 8(4)`

§§ `Regulation 5: how a choice of lump sum or survivor's pension may be made`

-- Gloss: in writing to an office, or by telephone to a number, that the Secretary of
-- State has specified in writing; but in writing only, where the Secretary of State
-- directs that in the particular case.
-- src:66 | (2) The manner is—
-- src:67 | (a) in writing to an office which is specified to the person in writing by the Secretary of State as accepting any such choice; or
-- src:68 | (b) by telephone to a telephone number which is specified to the person in writing by the Secretary of State as accepting any such choice.
-- src:69 | (3) The person must use the manner set out in paragraph (2)(a) where the Secretary of State directs in any particular case that that manner must be used.
@ref Regulation 5(2) and (3) (src:66-69)
GIVEN manner IS A MannerOfNotice
      `the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 5(2) and (3): the manner is one the Regulations accept` manner `the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case` MEANS
    CONSIDER manner
    WHEN `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `by telephone to a number specified in writing by the Secretary of State` THEN NOT (`the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case`)
    WHEN `in another manner` THEN FALSE

-- Regulation 5(1) only states that the regulation applies to a person within section
-- 8(1) of the 2014 Act and to a choice under section 8(2).
GIVEN `the person falls within section 8(1) of the 2014 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      manner IS A MannerOfNotice
      `the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`regulation 5: the choice is made in the manner required` `the person falls within section 8(1) of the 2014 Act` manner `the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case` MEANS
    IF `the person falls within section 8(1) of the 2014 Act`
    THEN JUST (`regulation 5(2) and (3): the manner is one the Regulations accept` manner `the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 6: changing a choice of lump sum or survivor's pension`

DECLARE AlterationFacts HAS
    `the person who made the choice has since died` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an application is made to alter the choice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date of the application` IS A DATE
    `the date in the notification issued by the Secretary of State confirming the choice` IS A DATE
    `the last day of any longer period that the Secretary of State considers reasonable` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the manner of the application` IS A MannerOfNotice
    `the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the choice the application asks for` IS A PaymentChoice
    `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date on which the repayment in full was completed` IS A DATE
    `that amount was repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount that would be paid by way of a state pension under section 9 of the 2014 Act` IS A NUMBER
    `the amount that would be paid as a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act` IS A NUMBER
    `a previous alteration has been made in respect of the same deferral` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the choice has been treated as made under regulation 30(5G) or (5H) of the Claims and Payments Regulations 1987` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The period in (c): three months starting on the date in the notification, or the
-- longer period the Secretary of State considers reasonable.
-- src:78 | (c) the application is made within—
-- src:79 | (i) the period of three months starting on the date in the notification issued by the Secretary of State which confirms the choice that has been made; or
-- src:80 | (ii) such longer period as the Secretary of State considers reasonable in any particular case;
@ref Regulation 6(2)(c) (src:78-80)
GIVEN facts IS A AlterationFacts
GIVETH A DATE
`regulation 6(2)(c): the last day of the period within which the application must be made` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `the last day of any longer period that the Secretary of State considers reasonable`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN threeMonthsEnd
    WHEN JUST longerEnd THEN IF longerEnd GREATER THAN threeMonthsEnd THEN longerEnd ELSE threeMonthsEnd
    WHERE
        threeMonthsEnd MEANS `the last day of a period of months starting on` (facts's `the date in the notification issued by the Secretary of State confirming the choice`) 3

@ref Regulation 6(2)(c) (src:78-80)
GIVEN facts IS A AlterationFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 6(2)(c): the application is made within the period` facts MEANS
        facts's `the date of the application` AT LEAST facts's `the date in the notification issued by the Secretary of State confirming the choice`
    AND facts's `the date of the application` AT MOST `regulation 6(2)(c): the last day of the period within which the application must be made` facts

-- Gloss: (d) the application is made in the manner regulation 5(2) allows, writing only
-- where the Secretary of State directs.
-- src:81 | (d) the application is made in the manner set out in—
-- src:82 | (i) regulation 5(2)(a), where the Secretary of State directs in any particular case that the manner in regulation 5(2)(a) must be used; or
-- src:83 | (ii) regulation 5(2)(a) or (b), in all other cases;
@ref Regulation 6(2)(d) (src:81-83)
GIVEN facts IS A AlterationFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 6(2)(d): the application is made in the manner required` facts MEANS
    `regulation 5(2) and (3): the manner is one the Regulations accept` (facts's `the manner of the application`) (facts's `the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case`)

-- Gloss: (e) an alteration TO a state pension needs the lump sum already paid to have
-- been repaid in full, in the original currency, and within the (c) period.
-- Where no lump sum was paid there is nothing to repay (fork F11).
-- Which period "mentioned in sub-paragraph (c)" is meant is not clear; the later end
-- of the two limbs of (c) is taken (fork F12).
-- src:84 | (e) where the application is to alter the choice so that it becomes a choice to be paid a state pension under section 9 of the 2014 Act, any amount paid by way of (or on account of) a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act has been repaid to the Secretary of State—
-- src:85 | (i) in full;
-- src:86 | (ii) within the period mentioned in sub-paragraph (c); and
-- src:87 | (iii) in the currency in which that amount was originally paid;
@ref Regulation 6(2)(e) (src:84-87)
GIVEN facts IS A AlterationFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 6(2)(e): where the alteration is to a state pension, any lump sum has been repaid` facts MEANS
    IF facts's `the choice the application asks for` EQUALS `a state pension`
    THEN (   NOT (facts's `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act`)
          OR (       facts's `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full`
                 AND facts's `that amount was repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid`
                 AND facts's `the date on which the repayment in full was completed` AT MOST `regulation 6(2)(c): the last day of the period within which the application must be made` facts))
    ELSE TRUE

-- Gloss: (f) an alteration TO a lump sum needs the state pension already paid to be
-- worth less than the lump sum.
-- src:88 | (f) where the application is to alter the choice so that it becomes a choice to be paid a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act, any amount paid by way of (or on account of) a state pension under section 9 of the 2014 Act would be less than the amount which would be paid as a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act;
@ref Regulation 6(2)(f) (src:88)
GIVEN facts IS A AlterationFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 6(2)(f): where the alteration is to a lump sum, the state pension paid is less than the lump sum` facts MEANS
    IF facts's `the choice the application asks for` EQUALS `a lump sum`
    THEN facts's `the amount that would be paid by way of a state pension under section 9 of the 2014 Act` LESS THAN facts's `the amount that would be paid as a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act`
    ELSE TRUE

-- Paragraph (2) lists (a) to (h) with "and" before (h): all of them are required.
-- src:75 | (2) The circumstances referred to in paragraph (1) are—
-- src:76 | (a) the person who made the choice has not subsequently died;
-- src:77 | (b) an application is made to alter the choice;
@ref Regulation 6(2)(a) and (b) (src:76-77)
GIVEN facts IS A AlterationFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 6(2)(a) and (b): the person is alive and an application is made` facts MEANS
        NOT (facts's `the person who made the choice has since died`)
    AND facts's `an application is made to alter the choice`

-- src:89 | (g) no previous alteration has been made under this regulation in respect of the same deferral mentioned in section 8(1)(c) of the 2014 Act; and
-- src:90 | (h) the choice has not been treated as made under regulation 30(5G) or (5H) of the Social Security (Claims and Payments) Regulations 1987 (payments on death) .
@ref Regulation 6(2)(g) and (h) (src:89-90)
GIVEN facts IS A AlterationFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 6(2)(g) and (h): no earlier alteration, and the choice was not treated as made under the 1987 Regulations` facts MEANS
        NOT (facts's `a previous alteration has been made in respect of the same deferral`)
    AND NOT (facts's `the choice has been treated as made under regulation 30(5G) or (5H) of the Claims and Payments Regulations 1987`)

-- src:71 | (1) Any choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act to be paid—
-- src:72 | (a) a lump sum under section 8 of that Act; or
-- src:73 | (b) a state pension under section 9 of that Act,
-- src:74 | may be altered in the circumstances specified in paragraph (2).
@ref Regulation 6(1) (src:71-74)
GIVEN facts IS A AlterationFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` facts MEANS
        `regulation 6(2)(a) and (b): the person is alive and an application is made` facts
    AND `regulation 6(2)(c): the application is made within the period` facts
    AND `regulation 6(2)(d): the application is made in the manner required` facts
    AND `regulation 6(2)(e): where the alteration is to a state pension, any lump sum has been repaid` facts
    AND `regulation 6(2)(f): where the alteration is to a lump sum, the state pension paid is less than the lump sum` facts
    AND `regulation 6(2)(g) and (h): no earlier alteration, and the choice was not treated as made under the 1987 Regulations` facts

-- Gloss: where the alteration is to a lump sum and the pension already paid is less
-- than that lump sum, the pension paid is treated as part-payment of the lump sum.
-- src:91 | (3) Where the circumstance in paragraph (2)(f) applies, any amount paid by way of (or on account of) a state pension under section 9 of the 2014 Act in respect of the deferral mentioned in section 8(1)(c) of the 2014 Act for which the choice was originally made is to be treated as having been paid on account of the lump sum to be paid under section 8 of the 2014 Act.
@ref Regulation 6(3) (src:91)
GIVEN facts IS A AlterationFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 6(3): the state pension already paid is treated as paid on account of the lump sum` facts MEANS
        facts's `the choice the application asks for` EQUALS `a lump sum`
    AND facts's `the amount that would be paid by way of a state pension under section 9 of the 2014 Act` LESS THAN facts's `the amount that would be paid as a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act`

§§ `Regulation 7: how entitlement to a state pension may be suspended`

-- Gloss: to "suspend" is to pause a state pension already in payment (and earn an
-- increase for the pause). The person must be entitled, and must give notice in
-- the manner (2) and (3) allow.
-- src:94 | (2) The manner in which the notice must be given is—
-- src:95 | (a) in writing to an office which is specified to the person in writing by the Secretary of State as accepting any such notice; or
-- src:96 | (b) by telephone to a telephone number which is specified to the person in writing by the Secretary of State as accepting any such notice.
-- src:97 | (3) But the person must use the manner set out in paragraph (2)(a) where the Secretary of State directs in any particular case that that manner must be used.
@ref Regulation 7(2) and (3) (src:94-97)
GIVEN manner IS A MannerOfNotice
      `the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 7(2) and (3): the notice is given in the manner required` manner `the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case` MEANS
    `regulation 5(2) and (3): the manner is one the Regulations accept` manner `the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case`

-- src:93 | (1) A person who has become entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act may opt to suspend their entitlement if they give notice to the Secretary of State.
@ref Regulation 7(1) (src:93)
GIVEN `the person has become entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person gives notice to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      manner IS A MannerOfNotice
      `the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 7: the person has opted to suspend their entitlement` `the person has become entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act` `the person gives notice to the Secretary of State` manner `the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case` MEANS
        `the person has become entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act`
    AND `the person gives notice to the Secretary of State`
    AND `regulation 7(2) and (3): the notice is given in the manner required` manner `the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case`

§§ `Regulation 8: the date from which a suspension begins`

-- Gloss: the person may name a start date from the day they give notice up to the end
-- of the 28 days starting with that day; otherwise the suspension starts when notice
-- is given. "28 days starting with" is counted by convention F1 (fork F13).
-- src:100 | (2) The date is any date which the person specifies that is—
-- src:101 | (a) not before the date on which the option was exercised; and
-- src:102 | (b) not after 28 days starting with the date on which the option was exercised.
@ref Regulation 8(2) (src:100-102)
GIVEN `the date on which the option was exercised` IS A DATE
      `the date the person specifies` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 8(2): the specified date is one the Regulations allow` `the date on which the option was exercised` `the date the person specifies` MEANS
        `the date the person specifies` AT LEAST `the date on which the option was exercised`
    AND `the date the person specifies` AT MOST `the last day of a period of days starting with` `the date on which the option was exercised` 28

-- src:99 | (1) Where a person exercises their option to suspend their entitlement to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act, the suspension takes effect from the date set out in this regulation.
-- src:103 | (3) Where the person does not specify a date in accordance with paragraph (2), the date is the date on which the option was exercised.
@ref Regulation 8(1) and (3) (src:99) (src:103)
GIVEN `the date on which the option was exercised` IS A DATE
      `the date the person specifies, if any` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`regulation 8: the date from which the suspension takes effect` `the date on which the option was exercised` `the date the person specifies, if any` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the person specifies, if any`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date on which the option was exercised`
    WHEN JUST specified THEN
        IF `regulation 8(2): the specified date is one the Regulations allow` `the date on which the option was exercised` specified
        THEN specified
        ELSE `the date on which the option was exercised`

§§ `Regulation 9: cancelling a suspension`

-- Gloss: a suspension is cancelled by claiming the state pension while it is
-- suspended. The cancellation can cover the whole or part of a past period of up to
-- 12 months before the date of the cancellation.
-- src:107 | (3) The past period mentioned in paragraph (1) is any period of up to 12 months before the date on which the person cancels the suspension.
@ref Regulation 9(3) (src:107)
GIVEN `the date on which the person cancels the suspension` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`regulation 9(3): the earliest day to which a cancellation can reach back` `the date on which the person cancels the suspension` MEANS
    `add months` `the date on which the person cancels the suspension` (0 MINUS 12)

-- src:105 | (1) Where a person has opted to suspend their entitlement to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act, the person may cancel the exercise of that option in relation to the whole of, or part of, a past period referred to in paragraph (3).
-- src:106 | (2) The person cancels the suspension by making a claim for their state pension whilst their state pension is suspended.
@ref Regulation 9(1) and (2) (src:105-106)
GIVEN `the person has opted to suspend their entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person claims their state pension whilst it is suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of that claim` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the period to be cancelled` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period to be cancelled` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 9: the suspension can be cancelled for the period` `the person has opted to suspend their entitlement` `the person claims their state pension whilst it is suspended` `the date of that claim` `the first day of the period to be cancelled` `the last day of the period to be cancelled` MEANS
        `the person has opted to suspend their entitlement`
    AND `the person claims their state pension whilst it is suspended`
    AND `the first day of the period to be cancelled` AT LEAST `regulation 9(3): the earliest day to which a cancellation can reach back` `the date of that claim`
    AND `the last day of the period to be cancelled` LESS THAN `the date of that claim`
    AND `the first day of the period to be cancelled` AT MOST `the last day of the period to be cancelled`

§§ `Regulation 10: the percentage for increases resulting from deferral`

-- Gloss: one-ninth of one per cent, which is one per cent for every nine weeks.
-- src:109 | For the purposes of section 17(4) of the 2014 Act (effect of pensioner postponing or suspending state pension), the specified percentage is one-ninth of 1%.
@ref Regulation 10 (src:109)
`regulation 10: the specified percentage for section 17(4) of the 2014 Act` MEANS 1% DIVIDED BY 9

§§ `Regulation 11: days which are not included in determining the period of deferral`

-- The benefits listed in regulation 11(2)(a).
DECLARE ListedBenefit IS ONE OF
    `state pension credit`
    `income support`
    `an income-related employment and support allowance`
    `an income-based jobseeker's allowance`
    `universal credit`
    `a carer's allowance`
    `the carer support payment component of carer support`
    `an unemployability supplement`
    `severe disablement allowance`
    `a widow's pension`
    `a widowed mother's allowance`
    `incapacity benefit`

DECLARE DayFacts HAS
    `the listed benefits that the deferred person received on the day` IS A LIST OF ListedBenefit
    `the listed benefits of which another person received an increase in respect of the deferred person on the day` IS A LIST OF ListedBenefit
    `that other person is married to, in a civil partnership with, or residing with the deferred person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deferred person would not, if their entitlement was not deferred, have been paid the state pension on the day because they were a prisoner` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:113 | (a) a day on which the person whose entitlement to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act is deferred has received any of the following benefits—
-- src:114 | (i) state pension credit under section 1 of the State Pension Credit Act 2002 (entitlement to state pension credit) ;
-- src:115 | (ii) income support under section 124 of the Contributions and Benefits Act (income support) ;
-- src:116 | (iii) an income-related employment and support allowance (which means an income-related allowance under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 (employment and support allowance) );
-- src:117 | (iv) an income-based jobseeker's allowance within the meaning in section 1(4) of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (the jobseeker's allowance) ;
-- src:118 | (v) universal credit under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (universal credit) ;
-- src:119 | (vi) a carer's allowance under section 70 of the Contributions and Benefits Act (carer's allowance) ;
-- src:120 | (via) the carer support payment component of carer support given in accordance with the Carer’s Assistance (Carer Support Payment) (Scotland) Regulations 2023 (“carer support payment”);
-- src:121 | (vii) an unemployability supplement within the meaning in regulation 2(1) of the Social Security (Overlapping Benefits) Regulations 1979 (interpretation) ;
-- src:122 | (viii) severe disablement allowance under section 68 of the Contributions and Benefits Act (entitlement and rate of severe disablement allowance) ;
-- src:123 | (ix) a widow's pension under section 39 of the Contributions and Benefits Act (rate of widowed mother's allowance and widow's pension) ;
-- src:124 | (x) a widowed mother's allowance under section 37 of the Contributions and Benefits Act (widowed mother's allowance) ;
-- src:125 | (xi) incapacity benefit under section 30A of the Contributions and Benefits Act (incapacity benefit: entitlement) ;
@ref Regulation 11(2)(a) (src:113-125)
GIVEN day IS A DayFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 11(2)(a): the deferred person received a listed benefit on the day` day MEANS
    NOT (null (day's `the listed benefits that the deferred person received on the day`))

-- src:126 | (b) a day on which a person—
-- src:127 | (i) has received an increase of any of the benefits mentioned in sub-paragraph (a) in respect of the person whose entitlement to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act is deferred; and
-- src:128 | (ii) is married to, in a civil partnership with or residing with the person whose entitlement to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act is deferred; or
@ref Regulation 11(2)(b) (src:126-128)
GIVEN day IS A DayFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 11(2)(b): another person received an increase of a listed benefit in respect of the deferred person` day MEANS
        NOT (null (day's `the listed benefits of which another person received an increase in respect of the deferred person on the day`))
    AND day's `that other person is married to, in a civil partnership with, or residing with the deferred person`

-- Regulations 2 and 3 answer this: feed `regulation 2(1): the state pension is not to
-- be paid for the day` (spr-part2-prisoners.l4) into the field.
-- src:129 | (c) a day on which the person whose entitlement to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act is deferred would not, if their entitlement was not deferred, be paid that state pension because they were a prisoner (see section 19 of the 2014 Act (prisoners) and regulations 2 and 3).
@ref Regulation 11(2)(c) (src:129)
GIVEN day IS A DayFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 11(2)(c): the deferred person would not have been paid because they were a prisoner` day MEANS
    day's `the deferred person would not, if their entitlement was not deferred, have been paid the state pension on the day because they were a prisoner`

-- src:111 | (1) In the circumstances set out in paragraph (2), a day does not count in determining a number of whole weeks for the purposes of section 17(3) of the 2014 Act.
-- src:112 | (2) The circumstances mentioned in paragraph (1) are where the day is—
@ref Regulation 11(1) and (2) (src:111-112)
GIVEN day IS A DayFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 11: the day does not count in determining the number of whole weeks` day MEANS
       `regulation 11(2)(a): the deferred person received a listed benefit on the day` day
    OR `regulation 11(2)(b): another person received an increase of a listed benefit in respect of the deferred person` day
    OR `regulation 11(2)(c): the deferred person would not have been paid because they were a prisoner` day

§§ `Regulation 12: part weeks treated as whole weeks`

-- Gloss: take the days of the deferral period, leave out the days that regulation 11
-- takes out, and count any left-over part of a week as a whole week.
-- NOTE (fork F14): section 17(3) of the 2014 Act, which asks for "whole weeks", is not
-- among the inputs; this is the arithmetic regulation 12 describes.
-- NOTHING means the days discounted exceed the days of the period, which the inputs
-- cannot truthfully say.
-- src:131 | (1) In the circumstances set out in paragraph (2), a part of a week is to be treated as a whole week for the purposes of section 17(3) of the 2014 Act.
-- src:132 | (2) The circumstances mentioned in paragraph (1) are where there is a part of a week in the total period during which the person's entitlement to a state pension was deferred, after any days have been discounted under regulation 11.
@ref Regulation 12 (src:131-132)
GIVEN deferral IS A DeferralPeriod
      `the number of days discounted under regulation 11` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`regulation 12: the number of whole weeks counted` deferral `the number of days discounted under regulation 11` MEANS
    IF counted LESS THAN 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (CEILING (counted DIVIDED BY 7))
    WHERE
        totalDays MEANS `the number of days from` (deferral's `first day of the deferral`) `to` (deferral's `last day of the deferral`) PLUS 1
        counted MEANS totalDays MINUS `the number of days discounted under regulation 11`

§§ `Regulation 12A: modification of the increment where the rate changes during deferral`

-- A modification period (regulation 12A(3) and (4)): first and last day.
DECLARE ModificationPeriod HAS
    `the first day of the modification period` IS A DATE
    `the last day of the modification period` IS A DATE

-- Gloss: a "non-uprating change" is a change in the weekly rate the person would have
-- had, other than the yearly up-rating. Regulation 12A applies only when there is one
-- inside the deferral period.
-- src:134 | (1) Subject to regulation 23, this regulation applies in cases where, at any time in the deferral period, the weekly rate of the person’s state pension, had the person’s entitlement not been deferred, would have changed otherwise than because of an up-rating increase (“a non-uprating change”).
@ref Regulation 12A(1) (src:134)
GIVEN deferral IS A DeferralPeriod
      `the dates of the non-uprating changes` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 12A(1): regulation 12A applies` deferral `the dates of the non-uprating changes` MEANS
    any (GIVEN changeDate YIELD changeDate AT LEAST deferral's `first day of the deferral` AND changeDate AT MOST deferral's `last day of the deferral`) `the dates of the non-uprating changes`

-- Gloss (3) and (4): the deferral is cut into stretches at each change. The first
-- stretch starts when the deferral starts and ends just before the first change; each
-- later stretch starts on a change and ends just before the next change, or at the end
-- of the deferral period. The dates must be given in date order (fork F15).
-- src:136 | (3) The first modification period begins at the start of the deferral period and ends immediately before the date of the first or only non-uprating change.
-- src:137 | (4) Further modification periods begin on the date of the most recent or only non-uprating change and end—
-- src:138 | (a) immediately before the end of the deferral period, where there is no subsequent non-uprating change; or
-- src:139 | (b) immediately before the date of the subsequent non-uprating change, where there is a subsequent non-uprating change.
@ref Regulation 12A(3) and (4) (src:136-139)
GIVEN start IS A DATE
      changes IS A LIST OF DATE
      `last day of the deferral` IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF ModificationPeriod
`regulation 12A(3) and (4): the modification periods from` start changes `last day of the deferral` MEANS
    CONSIDER changes
    WHEN EMPTY THEN
        LIST (ModificationPeriod WITH
                `the first day of the modification period` IS start
                `the last day of the modification period` IS `last day of the deferral`)
    WHEN nextChange FOLLOWED BY laterChanges THEN
        (ModificationPeriod WITH
            `the first day of the modification period` IS start
            `the last day of the modification period` IS nextChange MINUS 1)
        FOLLOWED BY (`regulation 12A(3) and (4): the modification periods from` nextChange laterChanges `last day of the deferral`)

-- Gloss (2): for each modification period the increment is the specified percentage
-- (regulation 10) of the weekly rate the person would have had immediately before the
-- end of that period. How many of the counted weeks belong to which period is not
-- said (fork F16); the weeks for the period are an input.
-- src:135 | (2) Section 17(4) of the 2014 Act (amount of an increment for pensioner postponing or suspending state pension) is modified to provide that the amount of an increment for each modification period is equal to a percentage specified in regulations of the weekly rate of the state pension to which the person, if their entitlement had not been deferred, would have been entitled immediately before the end of the modification period.
@ref Regulation 12A(2) (src:135)
GIVEN `the whole weeks counted in the modification period` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly rate the person would have had immediately before the end of the modification period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 12A(2): the increment for a modification period` `the whole weeks counted in the modification period` `the weekly rate the person would have had immediately before the end of the modification period` MEANS
    `regulation 10: the specified percentage for section 17(4) of the 2014 Act`
        TIMES `the whole weeks counted in the modification period`
        TIMES `the weekly rate the person would have had immediately before the end of the modification period`

-- Where regulation 12A does not apply, section 17(4) of the 2014 Act (not in the
-- inputs) fixes the reference rate; it is taken here as an input and the increase as
-- the specified percentage of it for each counted week (fork F14).
@ref Regulation 10 (src:109)
GIVEN `the whole weeks counted` IS A NUMBER
      `the reference weekly rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 10: the weekly increase for the weeks counted` `the whole weeks counted` `the reference weekly rate` MEANS
    `regulation 10: the specified percentage for section 17(4) of the 2014 Act` TIMES `the whole weeks counted` TIMES `the reference weekly rate`
